// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/own/shared.gopp %S/Inputs/own/shared.out
// RUN: %if qemu-aarch64 %{ %gopp build -test-intrinsics -target=linux/arm64 -crt-dir=%aarch64_sysroot/lib %S/Inputs/own/shared.gopp -o %t.arm64 %}
// RUN: %if qemu-aarch64 %{ %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --qemu %aarch64_sysroot %t.arm64 %S/Inputs/own/shared.out %}
// GOLDEN: by-hand
// P04.09: the shared handles (OWN-C3, TYP-5, CLO-2): interface boxes, func
// values' environments and closure cells are counted, and every allocation
// is freed by the last copy (counting allocator of the test intrinsics); a
// value in a box and a variable a closure captured are dropped once, when
// the last holder goes (the `drop` prints); a method value of a `move`
// receiver owns it (the call takes it, an uncalled one drops it); an
// interface argument the callee only looks at allocates nothing and one it
// keeps is copied into a box once (TYP-7); the results of a call and the
// variadic packs end with their statement. `ninja check-run-leaks` runs it
// under the address and leak sanitizers. See Inputs/own/shared.gopp.
